  <section>
    <title>Operating system support</title>
    <para>
      &s4h; is supported on &productnameshort; 15 and 16. &netweaver; is only supported on
      &productnameshort; 15.
    </para>
    <table xml:id="table-os-support-s4hana-nw" pgwide="1">
      <title>OS support for HA solutions for &s4hana; and &nwshort;</title>
      <tgroup cols="4">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>OS release</entry>
            <entry>&s4hana;</entry>
            <entry>&nwshort;</entry>
            <entry>Simple Mount file system structure</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>&productnameshort; 16</entry>
            <entry>Supported</entry>
            <entry>Non-supported</entry>
            <entry>Mandatory</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>&productnameshort; 15</entry>
            <entry>Supported</entry>
            <entry>Supported</entry>
            <entry>Supported</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sap-ha-solutions-for-s4hana-overview">
    <title>&s4hana; based on ABAP Platform 1809 or newer</title>
    <para>
      &ensa2long; (&ensa2;) is the successor to &ensa1long; (&ensa1;). Starting from
      ABAP Platform 1809, &ensa2long; is the default installation. The use of the new &ensa2long;
      and Enqueue Replicator 2 provides an improved &ha; architecture with robust and fast
      replication and failover.
    </para>
    <figure xml:id="fig-sap-ha-solutions-for-s4hana">
      <title>&s4h; based on ABAP Platform 1809 or newer</title>
      <mediaobject>
        <imageobject role="fo">
        <imagedata fileref="ensa2.svg" width="100%"/>
        </imageobject>
        <imageobject role="html">
        <imagedata fileref="ensa2.svg" width="100%"/>
        </imageobject>
        <textobject role="description">
        <phrase>
          &ensa2; two-node cluster configuration
        </phrase>
        </textobject>
      </mediaobject>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section xml:id="sap-ha-solutions-for-nw-overview">
    <title>&nwshort; based on ABAP Platform 1709 or older</title>
    <para>
      Under the &ensa1long; (&ensa1;), the ASCS has to fail over to the
      cluster node where the active ERS is running, because it needs to
      access the shared memory that stores the enqueue replication table.
    </para>
    <figure xml:id="fig-sap-ha-solutions-for-nw">
      <title>&netweaver; based on ABAP Platform 1709 or older</title>
